{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJWJTTED7HJDmzJ9y8UP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A stable set exists exactly when K is even. For K = 2h there is exactly one: {(0,h,h), (h,0,h), (h,h,0)}, the grid version of von Neumann and Morgenstern's symmetric solution. For odd K there are none.\n\nI searched every possible set for K = 2 to 11 and the results match this. The written proof in `/work/answer.md` covers every K ≥ 2. argon reviewed it and agreed. We both marked FINAL on the board and I wrote `/work/SUBMIT`.\n\nHow the proof goes:\n1. **When neither of two allocations dominates the other:** this happens exactly when they give the same amount to exactly one player. argon found this independently.\n2. **Shape of a set with no internal domination:** using step 1, every such set either lies on a single line (one player always gets the same amount c) or is a \"triangle\" of three points: a fixed allocation c, with s units taken from (or added to) one player at a time.\n3. **Lines fail:** allocations where that player gets c+1 are never dominated. Beating them would require giving the other two players two extra units between them, and only one is available. This is why the continuum's \"discriminatory\" solutions don't survive on the grid. When c = K, the point (1, 0, K−1) is never dominated instead.\n4. **Triangles fail except the symmetric one:** I construct an undominated allocation outside the set in each case: points added to c with s ≥ 2, with s = 1, and points taken from c when c ≠ (s,s,s). The remaining case, c = (s,s,s), forces K = 2s.\n5. **The symmetric set is stable:** I proved this directly, and the checker confirms it for K = 2, 4, 10 and 12.\n\nThe search script is `/work/opus/enum.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":141,"cache_read_input_tokens":31913,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":141,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62d98eb6-7775-4850-8689-de4ca26e51e6","uuid":"7dc40a9a-e96b-4c27-97c9-4b40dc376317","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:04:20.358Z","request_id":"req_011CgJWJT79eydd2bkbe9G6k"}
